      "node_id": "kg_doc_6",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: Ambroise Thomas. Charles Louis Ambroise Thomas (5 August 1811 – 12 February 1896) was a French composer, best known for his operas \"Mignon\" (1866) and \"Hamlet\" (1868, after Shakespeare) and as Director of the Conservatoire de Paris from 1871 till his death.",
